@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# draft-advisor-master-data: Read advisor master data from the ERP
+
+- **Jira:** none yet (direct request)
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: new ERP port operation and payload contract. The dependency `identity` → `integration` is new in code but already in architecture section 4)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** <GitHub login> <YYYY-MM-DD>
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: integration (public API `readAdvisor`), `erp-port` (operation `readAdvisor`), `erp-fake` (seed advisor), `apps/worker` (wiring)
+- **ADR:** [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-advisor-master-data-read.md)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data that the ERP leads. The `identity` module exposes it, read through `integration` (T3-D-005).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+The request has no acceptance criterion of its own. The change keeps these:
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T3-AC-001 | `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts`, `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts`, `packages/core/src/integration/integration.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `identity`: `createIdentity({ repo, bus, integration, clock })`; `.getAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<Advisor | null>`; type `Advisor`; invariant "advisor master data is read live, not stored, with source version and read time (ADR-0017)". T3-AC-001 stays owned by `integration`; identity's tests cite it because they check the read path. `integration`: `Integration.readAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData> | null>`. `erp-port`: `AdvisorMasterData`. `erp-fake`: `fakeAdvisors`.
+- **Contracts:** ERP port operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber)` → `AdvisorMasterData | null`. Payload `{ advisorNumber: /^B\d{5}$/, givenName, familyName, email (e-mail), active: boolean, sourceVersion }`. No events.
+- **Schema:** none. Nothing is stored.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- `getAdvisor` returns `{ advisorNumber, givenName, familyName, email, active, sourceVersion, readAt }`: the `ErpRead` envelope flattened, without `source` (always `erp`). As requested.
+- `identity` depends on `Pick<Integration, "readAdvisor">`, not the whole API, so its tests use a small stub and never load an adapter.
+- The read carries `sourceVersion` and `readAt` through the existing `ErpRead<T>` envelope (the pattern of T2-D-009, which itself speaks of basket-line copies).
+- An ERP outage is not caught: `getAdvisor` rejects with `ErpUnavailableError` and the caller decides the fallback ([ERP conventions](../../conventions/erp.md)).
+- No validation of the advisor number format in `identity`; an unknown or malformed number gives `null` from the ERP.
+- Fake advisor `B20001` (Berta Beraterin, `berta.beraterin@example.test`, active, `v2`); it is the advisor of fake customer `K100001`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- A read copy of advisors in `erp_copy` and its sync.
+- A link from an advisor to a person record, roles, the advisor structure.
+- A head office screen or HTTP endpoint.
+
+## Open questions
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
